// Memory Hierarchy Levels (Speed/Cost Tradeoffs)
Registers (L0) [Fastest, Smallest]
L1 Cache (SRAM)
L2 Cache (SRAM)
L3 Cache (SRAM)
Main Memory (DRAM)
Solid State Drive (SSD)
Hard Disk Drive (HDD) [Slowest, Largest]

// Volatility
SRAM/DRAM: Volatile (Data lost on power loss)
SSD/HDD: Non-Volatile (Persistent storage)

// Disk Latency Components (HDD Access Time)
Access_Time =
    Seek_Time         // Moving arm to cylinder (Dominant)
  + Rotation_Latency  // Waiting for sector alignment
  + Transfer_Time     // Reading data from surface

// Caching Strategy: Locality and Block Size
#define CACHE_LINE_SIZE 64 // Typical transfer unit

// Spatial Locality: Fetch X and nearby neighbors
// Temporal Locality: Keep frequently used X

// Cache Hit (Fast) vs. Cache Miss (Slow, must fetch from lower level)
Miss Penalty: Time to retrieve block from next slower level.
